  "about": "who sees a picker tile's picture if you send it from this room, and whether the tile is offered at all (shared/emote-mark.ts, docs/emote-law.md offer + tile mark). every client runs every case against its own code. a world is the law's: rooms, globals and people, every list shuffled by the runner. a tile is an emote and the tier it sits in (where the law's offer found it). `pic` is the picture a copy shows when it is another's (a saved copy of a 7tv or twitch emote has its own id and the picture's `pic`); `hash` makes two uploads of ours one picture. expect: offered = the room does not answer the tile's word with another picture; mark = the one corner letter ('' none); kind = everyone | ext | heatsync; as = whose picture it goes out as (hs when only heatsync users see it); tier = where what it ships sits (the room's, yours, a global, not loaded here), the tile's own when the word has no answer. a runner that meets a kind or a field it does not know must fail, never skip.",
